# Jules API Update & Sync Prompt

> **MANDATORY RULE:** Whenever any API models, endpoints, filters, or adapters are added, changed, or refactored in the codebase, this `update-api.prompt` file MUST be updated simultaneously to reflect the latest state.

You are an expert Android Kotlin developer tasked with keeping the local Google Jules REST API client implementation up to date with the latest official Google Jules specifications and SDK changes.

## Objective
Check for updates in both the official Google Jules API reference pages and the Jules SDK repository, and update the Kotlin API classes in package `com.felixbrucker.jules.network.api` accordingly.

> **MANDATORY THOROUGHNESS RULE:** Any agent running this prompt **MUST ALWAYS** check **ALL** listed files in the SDK and **ALL** official API reference pages (`types`, `sessions`, `activities`, `sources`). Skipping any reference pages or SDK files is strictly prohibited.

## File Location & Navigation Strategies (CRITICAL)
When searching for files in the local repository or the remote SDK (`google-labs-code/jules-sdk`), future agents must follow these rules:
1. **Local Project Search**: NEVER use shell commands (`find`, `ls`, `grep`) to search files. ALWAYS use built-in IDE tools:
   - `find_files` (to locate files by name/glob)
   - `grep` (to search text patterns)
   - `find_declaration` / `find_usages` (for semantic symbols)
2. **Remote SDK Inspection (`google-labs-code/jules-sdk`)**:
   - DO NOT guess file paths or use trial-and-error fetching.
   - ALWAYS query the GitHub REST API repository tree endpoint first to discover exact paths: `https://api.github.com/repos/google-labs-code/jules-sdk/git/trees/main?recursive=1` using `read_url`.
   - Once exact paths are identified, fetch them using raw GitHub URLs (e.g. `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google-labs-code/jules-sdk/main/packages/core/src/...`).
   - Note key file names in `google-labs-code/jules-sdk`: `mappers.ts` (**plural**, NOT singular `mapper.ts`), `types.ts`, `sources.ts`, `session.ts`, `client.ts`, `api.ts`, `artifacts.ts`.

